Several people have commented on the difficulty of knowing which
options are enabled.  If the hack-maintainers want to add the
following code to main.c or somewhere like that, the binary would
contain them in a form readable by "strings":
	/* in main.c, outside the main() routine */
	char *COMPILE_OPTIONS[] = {
	"Compile options =",
	#ifdef HARD
	"hard,",
	#endif
	#ifdef WIZARD
	"wizard,",
	#endif
	}
	/* in main() routine */
	(void) COMPILE_OPTIONS ;
Depending on how the patchlevel is represented, you could do
something similar with it.

